---
import '../../styles/diagram.css';
---

{/*
  The site's one interactive moment. This case study's claim is that a failover
  is a change in where a single endpoint points, not a change in every client
  application — so the reader gets to perform it and watch exactly one thing move.

  A checkbox plus sibling selectors: no JavaScript, no hydration, and the control
  is keyboard-operable and announced as a toggle for free. The reduced-motion
  rule in base.css already strips the transitions.
*/}
<figure class="diagram dr">
  <input type="checkbox" id="dr-failover" class="dr__input visually-hidden" />

  <div class="dr__bar">
    <label for="dr-failover" class="dr__toggle">Simulate failover</label>
  </div>

  <svg class="dr__svg" viewBox="0 0 720 372" role="img" aria-labelledby="dr-title dr-desc">
    <title id="dr-title">Network-of-brokers topology across three AWS regions</title>
    <desc id="dr-desc">
      Producers and consumers connect through a single endpoint. Brokers in Oregon, London
      and Ireland are joined as a network, so messages forward across the links. Normally
      the endpoint points at Oregon, which is active, while London and Ireland are passive.
      Turning on the failover toggle repoints the endpoint at London and makes it active,
      and Oregon becomes unreachable. Nothing else in the picture changes, which is the point.
    </desc>

    <!-- Endpoint. Producers and consumers are named inside it rather than as
         floating labels, which keeps the left edge clear. -->
    <path class="diagram__fill" d="M22 22 L251 23 L252 89 L23 88 Z"></path>
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M22 22 L251 23 L252 89 L23 88 Z"></path>
    <text class="diagram__label" x="40" y="51">single endpoint</text>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="40" y="71">producers and consumers</text>

    <!-- Endpoint to Oregon: the live path by default -->
    <path class="diagram__art dr-link dr-link--oregon" d="M96 89 C 97 120, 95 148, 96 190"></path>
    <path class="diagram__ink-fill dr-arrow dr-arrow--oregon" d="M96 198 L91 186 L101 186 Z"></path>
    <text class="diagram__meta dr-only-normal" x="106" y="142">points here</text>

    <!-- Endpoint to London: dashed and waiting by default, live once failed over -->
    <path
      class="diagram__accent dr-link dr-link--london"
      d="M252 58 C 330 60, 352 112, 356 189"></path>
    <path class="diagram__accent-fill dr-arrow dr-arrow--london" d="M356 198 L351 186 L361 186 Z"
    ></path>
    <text class="diagram__meta dr-accent-text dr-only-normal" x="268" y="126">on failover</text>
    <text class="diagram__meta dr-accent-text dr-only-failed" x="268" y="126">points here</text>

    <!-- Region brokers -->
    <path class="diagram__fill dr-fill dr-fill--oregon" d="M22 190 L171 191 L172 259 L23 258 Z"
    ></path>
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M22 190 L171 191 L172 259 L23 258 Z"></path>
    <text class="diagram__label" x="40" y="219">Oregon</text>
    <text class="diagram__meta dr-only-normal" x="40" y="239">active</text>
    <text class="diagram__meta dr-only-failed" x="40" y="239">unreachable</text>

    <path class="diagram__fill dr-fill dr-fill--london" d="M282 191 L431 190 L430 259 L281 258 Z"
    ></path>
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M282 191 L431 190 L430 259 L281 258 Z"></path>
    <text class="diagram__label" x="300" y="219">London</text>
    <text class="diagram__meta dr-only-normal" x="300" y="239">passive</text>
    <text class="diagram__meta dr-only-failed" x="300" y="239">active</text>

    <!-- Ireland is identical in both states, which is itself the information -->
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M542 190 L691 191 L690 259 L541 258 Z"></path>
    <text class="diagram__label" x="560" y="219">Ireland</text>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="560" y="239">passive</text>

    <!-- Network of brokers: the links that carry messages between regions -->
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M172 224 C 212 223, 244 225, 281 224"></path>
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M431 224 C 471 225, 503 223, 541 224"></path>
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M97 259 C 100 316, 190 334, 356 335 C 522 336, 612 317, 616 259"></path>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="286" y="356">network of brokers</text>
  </svg>

  <p class="dr__status" aria-live="polite">
    <span class="dr-only-normal">
      Oregon is serving traffic. London and Ireland are attached to the network and idle.
    </span>
    <span class="dr-only-failed">
      Oregon is gone and London is serving traffic. One endpoint moved — no client
      application changed, and nothing had to be replayed by hand.
    </span>
  </p>

  <figcaption class="diagram__caption">
    The managed replication feature didn’t cover this region combination, so the brokers are
    joined as a network instead. Clients hold one endpoint, which is what makes failover a
    single deliberate change rather than a change in every application.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .dr__bar {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .dr__toggle {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-sm);
    border: var(--hairline) solid var(--rule-strong);
    font-family: var(--face-mono);
    font-size: var(--step-mono-sm);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-mono);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    cursor: pointer;
    user-select: none;
    transition:
      color var(--duration) var(--ease),
      border-color var(--duration) var(--ease);
  }

  .dr__toggle:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
    border-color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  /* The checkbox is visually hidden but still focusable, so the ring has to be
     drawn on the label it controls. */
  .dr__input:focus-visible ~ .dr__bar .dr__toggle {
    outline: var(--focus-ring) solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .dr__input:checked ~ .dr__bar .dr__toggle {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .dr__status {
    max-width: var(--grid-measure);
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-family: var(--face-mono);
    font-size: var(--step-mono-xs);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* Both states are authored into the SVG and swapped, because CSS cannot
     rewrite the content of an SVG text node. */
  .dr-only-failed {
    display: none;
  }

  .dr__input:checked ~ .dr__svg .dr-only-normal,
  .dr__input:checked ~ .dr__status .dr-only-normal {
    display: none;
  }

  .dr__input:checked ~ .dr__svg .dr-only-failed,
  .dr__input:checked ~ .dr__status .dr-only-failed {
    display: inline;
  }

  .dr-accent-text {
    fill: var(--accent);
  }

  .dr-fill,
  .dr-link,
  .dr-arrow {
    transition:
      opacity var(--duration) var(--ease),
      stroke var(--duration) var(--ease);
  }

  /* Default: Oregon is live, London is the waiting path. */
  .dr-fill--london,
  .dr-arrow--london {
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .dr-link--london {
    stroke-dasharray: 5 6;
  }

  /* Failed over: the endpoint moves, and only the endpoint moves. */
  .dr__input:checked ~ .dr__svg .dr-fill--oregon,
  .dr__input:checked ~ .dr__svg .dr-arrow--oregon {
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .dr__input:checked ~ .dr__svg .dr-link--oregon {
    stroke: var(--rule-strong);
    stroke-dasharray: 3 5;
  }

  .dr__input:checked ~ .dr__svg .dr-fill--london,
  .dr__input:checked ~ .dr__svg .dr-arrow--london {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .dr__input:checked ~ .dr__svg .dr-link--london {
    stroke-dasharray: none;
  }
</style>
